<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.4 </span>Evaluation Protocol</h4>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">High-order ToM generalization is referred to as the ability of a model that has mastered reasoning at a small depth <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> to extrapolate to previously unseen larger depths <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.
This transition is interpreted as a qualitative leap in core ToM competence.
Formally, for any fixed complexity variable <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, we partition the data set distribution <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{\{(n,m),q,k\mid\mathcal{L}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{\{(n,m),q,k\mid\mathcal{L}\}}</annotation></semantics></math> into training set <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> for learning and test set <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> for generalization:</p>
<table id="S4.E2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E2X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{l}=\{D\sim\mathbb{P}_{((n,m),q,k^{\prime}\mid\mathcal{L})}\mid k^{\prime}\in\mathcal{K}_{l}\},~~\mathcal{D}_{g}=\{D\sim\mathbb{P}_{((n,m),q,k^{\prime}\mid\mathcal{L})}\mid k^{\prime}\in\mathcal{K}_{g}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo rspace="0.827em">,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{D}_{l}=\{D\sim\mathbb{P}_{((n,m),q,k^{\prime}\mid\mathcal{L})}\mid k^{\prime}\in\mathcal{K}_{l}\},~~\mathcal{D}_{g}=\{D\sim\mathbb{P}_{((n,m),q,k^{\prime}\mid\mathcal{L})}\mid k^{\prime}\in\mathcal{K}_{g}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E2Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{where}\quad\mathcal{K}_{g}\cup\mathcal{K}_{l}=\mathcal{K},~\mathcal{K}_{g}\cap\mathcal{K}_{l}=\emptyset,~\bm{\min(\mathcal{K}_{g})&gt;\max(\mathcal{K}_{l})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐦𝐢𝐧</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓚</mi><mi>𝒈</mi></msub><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold">&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>𝐦𝐚𝐱</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝓚</mi><mi>𝒍</mi></msub><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{where}\quad\mathcal{K}_{g}\cup\mathcal{K}_{l}=\mathcal{K},~\mathcal{K}_{g}\cap\mathcal{K}_{l}=\emptyset,~\bm{\min(\mathcal{K}_{g})&gt;\max(\mathcal{K}_{l})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The generalization process in general can be denoted as <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{l}\xrightarrow{k\uparrow}\mathcal{D}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.700em">k</mi><mo mathsize="0.700em" stretchy="false">↑</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mover><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>g</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{l}\xrightarrow{k\uparrow}\mathcal{D}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We varied task complexity to construct parallel experimental groups, ensuring the robustness of our evaluation. Specifically, we set <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\{4,5,6\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\{4,5,6\}</annotation></semantics></math> to cover three node scales and then specified the number of edges <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. Our objective was to maintain a moderate graph density under each <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math> configuration, thereby avoiding cases where overly sparse graphs yielded insufficient character interactions, while overly dense graphs led to information overload.
Specifically, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Easley et al. [2010]</a></cite>, we define the graph density as</p>
<table id="S4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{density}(G)=\frac{m}{\binom{n}{2}}=\frac{2m}{n(n-1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>density</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{density}(G)=\frac{m}{\binom{n}{2}}=\frac{2m}{n(n-1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and restrict the candidate <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math> configurations to the medium-density range <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{density}(G)\in[0.40,0.80]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>density</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.40</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.80</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{density}(G)\in[0.40,0.80]</annotation></semantics></math>.
The final selected configurations are:
when <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=4</annotation></semantics></math> (density <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.67" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.67</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.67</annotation></semantics></math>);
when <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=5</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=7,8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=7,8</annotation></semantics></math> (densities <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.70,0.80" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.70</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.80</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.70,0.80</annotation></semantics></math>);
when <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=6</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=7,8,9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=7,8,9</annotation></semantics></math> (densities <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.47,0.53,0.60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.47</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.53</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.60</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.47,0.53,0.60</annotation></semantics></math>).
These densities are evenly distributed within the “neither too sparse nor too dense” interval.
In addition, <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> determines the search space of the final options: if a scene contains <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S4.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000B3;">containers</span>, the random accuracy is <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/q</annotation></semantics></math>. We set <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in{3,4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in{3,4}</annotation></semantics></math> to vary this baseline.
Overall, we set the spaces of all complexity variables as follows:</p>
<table id="S4.E4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E4X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(n,m)\in\mathcal{S}=\{(4,4),(5,7),(5,8),(6,7),(6,8),(6,9)\},~~~~q\in\mathcal{Q}=\{3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.487em">,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(n,m)\in\mathcal{S}=\{(4,4),(5,7),(5,8),(6,7),(6,8),(6,9)\},~~~~q\in\mathcal{Q}=\{3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Based on this setting, we form <span id="S4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12 parallel experimental groups</span>, each corresponding to a unique configuration of <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((n,m),q)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((n,m),q)\in\mathcal{S}\times\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then we let <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}=\{1,2,3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}=\{1,2,3\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{l}=\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{l}=\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}_{g}=\{2,3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_{g}=\{2,3\}</annotation></semantics></math>, so within each group, our ToMNN was trained exclusively on <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> (first-order ToM) and subsequently tested on <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2,3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2,3</annotation></semantics></math> (second- and third-order ToM).
Regarding the dataset size under each group, the statistics are provided in Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.4 Evaluation Protocol ‣ 4 Method ‣ Spontaneous High-Order Generalization in Neural Theory-of-Mind Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, with further explanation in Section <a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Data Scale of 𝒟_{(𝑛,𝑚),𝑞,𝑘∣ℒ} ‣ 4 Method ‣ Spontaneous High-Order Generalization in Neural Theory-of-Mind Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:80%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T3.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S4.T3.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:113%;">Dataset sizes under different configurations <math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,m,q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,m,q)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S4.T3.8" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:73pt;vertical-align:-34.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-31.6pt,6.7pt) scale(0.845087668531298,0.845087668531298) ;">
<table id="S4.T3.8.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S4.T3.8.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Configuration</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Training Size</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Testing Size</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Configuration</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Training Size</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;">Testing Size</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.8.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(4,4,3)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1,306,368</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">93,312</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(6,7,3)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;" rowspan="6"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1,032,192</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;" rowspan="6"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">73,728</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.8.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(4,4,4)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(6,7,4)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.8.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(5,7,3)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;" rowspan="4"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1,161,216</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;" rowspan="4"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">82,944</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(6,8,3)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.8.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(5,8,3)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(6,8,4)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.8.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(5,7,4)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(6,9,3)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T3.8.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(5,8,4)</span></td>
<td id="S4.T3.8.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding:0.85pt 5.7pt;"><span id="S4.T3.8.1.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">(6,9,4)</span></td></tr>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5 </span>Data Scale of <math id="S4.SS5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\{(n,m),q,k\mid\mathcal{L}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\{(n,m),q,k\mid\mathcal{L}\}}</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In constructing the <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\{(n,m),q,k\mid\mathcal{L}\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\{(n,m),q,k\mid\mathcal{L}\}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we began with the initial variables <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{(n,m),q,k\mid\mathcal{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(n,m),q,k\mid\mathcal{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and two stages involved diversification: (1) <span id="S4.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">graph structure screening</span>, which ensured diversity in interaction topological structures, and (2) <span id="S4.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">scene generation</span>, which introduced diversity in semantic representations. Based on these, we defined and calculated the dataset size under all variable configurations <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{(n,m),q,k\mid\mathcal{L}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(n,m),q,k\mid\mathcal{L}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Topological Structure Expansion</h5>

<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">During the <span id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">graph structure screening</span> stage (Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Textual Concretization ‣ 4 Method ‣ Spontaneous High-Order Generalization in Neural Theory-of-Mind Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, Stage 1), all structures with <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> labeled nodes (each assigned a unique attribute) and <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> directed edges are required to satisfy the following validity conditions:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I4" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.9cm;">
<li id="S4.I4.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I4.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I4.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Acyclicity:</span> The graph contains no directed cycle.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I4.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I4.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I4.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I4.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Connectivity:</span> The graph contains no isolated nodes, <span id="S4.I4.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">i.e.</span>, each node must appear in at least one edge.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">First, for the <span id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Acyclicity</span>, we enforce this by fixing a canonical topological order <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\prec 2\prec\cdots\prec n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≺</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0.1389em">≺</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo lspace="0.1389em">≺</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\prec 2\prec\cdots\prec n</annotation></semantics></math> and only allowing edges to point backward in that order. The admissible edge set is</p>
<table id="S4.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E^{\star}=\{(j,i):1\preceq i\prec j\preceq n\},\qquad M=|E^{\star}|=\binom{n}{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≺</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E^{\star}=\{(j,i):1\preceq i\prec j\preceq n\},\qquad M=|E^{\star}|=\binom{n}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Each candidate graph is a subset <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E\subseteq E^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E\subseteq E^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|E|=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|E|=m</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under this topological order, and in accordance with the task-specific requirements (Section <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Textual Concretization ‣ 4 Method ‣ Spontaneous High-Order Generalization in Neural Theory-of-Mind Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>, Stage 2) during the <span id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">scene template generation</span> stage, a valid graph must further satisfy the following condition:</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="S4.I5" class="ltx_enumerate" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0.9cm;">
<li id="S4.I5.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S4.I5.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I5.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I5.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">Room-induced Closure:</span>
Let <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of nodes currently present in the “room” immediately before processing node <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.
The iteration begins with an empty room, <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{1}=\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{1}=\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>.
At each step <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=1,\dots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=1,\dots,n</annotation></semantics></math>, the following rules apply:</p>
<table id="S4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(Closure constraint)}\quad S_{v}\setminus\{v\}\subseteq P(v)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>(Closure constraint)</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(Closure constraint)}\quad S_{v}\setminus\{v\}\subseteq P(v),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(Room update)}\quad S_{v+1}=(S_{v}\cup P(v))\setminus\{v\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>(Room update)</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(Room update)}\quad S_{v+1}=(S_{v}\cup P(v))\setminus\{v\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.I5.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(v)=\{\,u:(u,v)\in E\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(v)=\{\,u:(u,v)\in E\,\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the parent set of <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.
In words, every individual already in the room (except <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> itself) must also be a parent of <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, and after <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is processed, the room is updated by admitting all of <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>’s parents and removing <math id="S4.I5.i3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> itself.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">With the above constraints, the room state evolves deterministically.
Since <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{v}\setminus\{v\}\subseteq P(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{v}\setminus\{v\}\subseteq P(v)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{v+1}=(S_{v}\cup P(v))\setminus\{v\}=P(v)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{v+1}=(S_{v}\cup P(v))\setminus\{v\}=P(v).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{v}=|P(v)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{v}=|P(v)|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{v}=|S_{v}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{v}=|S_{v}|</annotation></semantics></math>. This yields the recurrence</p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="s_{1}=0,\qquad s_{v+1}=r_{v},\qquad s_{v}\leq r_{v}\leq|V_{\succ v}|\quad(\forall v)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}=0,\qquad s_{v+1}=r_{v},\qquad s_{v}\leq r_{v}\leq|V_{\succ v}|\quad(\forall v),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\succ v}:=\{\,u\in V:v\prec u\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≺</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\succ v}:=\{\,u\in V:v\prec u\,\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of nodes that follow <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in the topological order, so <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V_{\succ v}|=n-v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V_{\succ v}|=n-v</annotation></semantics></math> under the canonical labeling.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">At each step <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, among the <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V_{\succ v}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V_{\succ v}|</annotation></semantics></math> potential parents of <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, exactly <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> are already present in the room and must be included; the remaining <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{v}-s_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{v}-s_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> parents can be freely selected from the <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> optional candidates.
Thus, the number of admissible choices for <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(v)</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}}{\,r_{v}-s_{v}\,}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}}{\,r_{v}-s_{v}\,}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Summing over all feasible parent-size sequences <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{v}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{v}\}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{v=1}^{n}r_{v}=m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{v=1}^{n}r_{v}=m</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the count of valid structures under a fixed topological order (before enforcing connectivity):</p>
<table id="S4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{0}^{\prime}(n,m)=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}r_{1},\dots,r_{n}\\
s_{1}=0,\ s_{v+1}=r_{v}\\
s_{v}\leq r_{v}\leq|V_{\succ v}|\\
\sum r_{v}=m\end{subarray}}\ \prod_{v=1}^{n}\binom{|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}}{\,r_{v}-s_{v}\,}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">v</mi></msub></mrow></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{0}^{\prime}(n,m)=\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}r_{1},\dots,r_{n}\\
s_{1}=0,\ s_{v+1}=r_{v}\\
s_{v}\leq r_{v}\leq|V_{\succ v}|\\
\sum r_{v}=m\end{subarray}}\ \prod_{v=1}^{n}\binom{|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}}{\,r_{v}-s_{v}\,}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, to eliminate isolated nodes, we apply an inclusion–exclusion principle over all subsets <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\subseteq V=\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\subseteq V=\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, enforcing that every <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in X</annotation></semantics></math> is isolated sets <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{u}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{u}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and removes <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> from all later candidate pools.
This shrinks the optional pool at step <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}-|X_{\succ v}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}-|X_{\succ v}|</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{\succ v}:=X\cap V_{\succ v}=\{\,u\in X:v\prec u\,\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>≺</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{\succ v}:=X\cap V_{\succ v}=\{\,u\in X:v\prec u\,\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The resulting count is</p>
<table id="S4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\prime}(n,m)=\sum_{X\subseteq V}(-1)^{|X|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}r_{1},\dots,r_{n}\\
s_{1}=0,\ s_{v+1}=r_{v}\\
s_{v}\leq r_{v}\leq|V_{\succ v}|-|X_{\succ v}|\\
r_{u}=0,\ \forall u\in X\\
\sum r_{v}=m\end{subarray}}\ \prod_{v=1}^{n}\binom{|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}-|X_{\succ v}|}{\,r_{v}-s_{v}\,}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.700em">r</mi><mi mathsize="0.710em">v</mi></msub></mrow></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≻</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\prime}(n,m)=\sum_{X\subseteq V}(-1)^{|X|}\sum_{\begin{subarray}{c}r_{1},\dots,r_{n}\\
s_{1}=0,\ s_{v+1}=r_{v}\\
s_{v}\leq r_{v}\leq|V_{\succ v}|-|X_{\succ v}|\\
r_{u}=0,\ \forall u\in X\\
\sum r_{v}=m\end{subarray}}\ \prod_{v=1}^{n}\binom{|V_{\succ v}|-s_{v}-|X_{\succ v}|}{\,r_{v}-s_{v}\,}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Because isomorphic graphs under different topological orders are treated as distinct, the final count is</p>
<table id="S4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(n,m)=n!\,N^{\prime}(n,m)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(n,m)=n!\,N^{\prime}(n,m).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Back to our experimental setup, we consider six <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math> configurations: <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(4,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(4,4)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(5,7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(5,7)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(5,8)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(5,8)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6,7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6,7)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6,8)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6,8)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(6,9)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(6,9)</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting these into the counting procedure described above yields the exact number of valid graph structures for each configuration, as shown in Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Topological Structure Expansion ‣ 4.5 Data Scale of 𝒟_{(𝑛,𝑚),𝑞,𝑘∣ℒ} ‣ 4 Method ‣ Spontaneous High-Order Generalization in Neural Theory-of-Mind Networks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. We observe that the total number of structures increases substantially with larger <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. To maintain consistency across all configurations, we adopt the minimum count, <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(4,4)=120" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>120</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(4,4)=120</annotation></semantics></math>, as the reference. Accordingly, <span id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">we restrict the dataset to 120 distinct structures (112 for training and 8 held out for testing).</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S4.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Number of valid DAG structures <math id="S4.T4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N^{\prime}(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N^{\prime}(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math> under a fixed topological order, and the final count <math id="S4.T4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(n,m)=n!\,N^{\prime}(n,m)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>!</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(n,m)=n!\,N^{\prime}(n,m)</annotation></semantics></math> when all topological orders are distinguished.</span></figcaption>
